Z||000000||Pontiaddict||07-07-2000||07:27 PM|||| <A HREF="http://cartalk.cars.com/Survey/Results/Psychographics/Caroscopes" TARGET=_blank>http://cartalk.cars.com/Survey/Results/Psychographics/Caroscopes</A> <P>While it said that I was a good match for my Fiero, It also said...<P>...there are some psychographic and/or demographic measures on which you differ from other Pontiac Fiero owners. For example, you are a bit too young to be driving this vehicle, and you care a bit too much about<BR> your car compared to other Pontiac Fiero owners...<P>I'm 19 and I said that I think the kind of car that I drive is very important so the other cars they recommend are...<P>1.Plymouth Duster<BR>2.Chevrolet Camaro<BR>3.Oldsmobile Cutlass<BR>4.Dodge Daytona<BR>5.Dodge Colt Vista<P>First of all, For someone who thinks that the kind of car they drive is important, why would they think that I would like a <B>Dodge Colt Vista!!!</B> I wouldn't be caught dead in any of those cars! Maybe the Camaro, but I'd never buy one being a "Potiaddict" and GM having a Poncho alternative. (One's sitting in my driveway.) Why wasn't a T/A in the list?<P>One reason, I have a crappy job so I don't make much! I think the Car Guys are stupid anyway. THEIR RADIO SHOW SUCKS! And the website relects on their stupidity.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||07-07-2000||09:57 PM||||Their humor is probably geared more toward us middle aged guys. It's all just a joke this Car-o-scope stuff. Don't take it too serious. You get pretty much the same results no matter what you put in. Personally, I like their radio show, but to each their own.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||07-08-2000||12:10 AM||||And another little thing to remember is that one of the guys owns a Dodge colt vista so that shows up on every result.  Not a big fan but my significant other is a regular listener.||||reg||1
